
      Alternating Screen Utility V0.93 (c)92 by Paul Spijkerman

Don't you know which logout screen to pick with all those little nets ? 
Or don't you want to install an other one each day ?
This little fully configurable utility whil do this for you.
Randomly or 1 by 1 from a Queue (count mode).
And not only logout screens but any screen you want.
It is written for a Xenolink BBS but can be used on every BBS Program.
In fact, I ported this program for use on the PC.


Usage:  path\altscr path\configfile

Option: -d   (Debug)
   The altscr executable has a fool proof parser and will give all
   the information you need if errors occur.
   But just in case you can specify the -d option to obtain extra
   Debug information.


Use this in a script after every call or once a day.

DON'T FORGET TO RENAME OR BACKUP YOUR LOGOUT.* SCREENS IF THEY
ARE ORIGINALS BECAUSE THIS PROGRAM WILL WRITE THEM OVER.

Because it is fully configurable it can be used for every
screen. And you can place all files in one directory
or whereever you want.

=====( The configuration file. )=======================

-commands:

/random              : Uses seconds from clock to choose a
                       screen randomly

/count               : uses a file in which a counter is kept.

/countfile           : place name of file after this command
path/countfilename     in which the counters should be kept
                       if you use more configuration files
                       don't forget to use different 
                       filenames in all of them.


The 3 commands named above can be placed anywhere in the config file,
the last one mentioned in the file will be used !


/input               : The source screen names
path/name1             Don't leave empty lines or comment between
path/name2             the command and the filenames
path/name3
#                    : Use a # to close the Queue !!!!


/output              : after this command the path and
path\name              name of the screen you want to
                       alternate is placed.


For every screen you want to rotate you need a /input and /output
command in the config file.
In one config file you can rotate up to 80 screens.
You can use a variable number of screens after every each /input
command, for each /input-/output command combination a counter is kept.


=======( Installing )================================

(This is only an example for xenolink, you can vary every dir name.)

-Make a directory named altscr in the doors directory.

    makedir doors:altscr

-Place a assign command in your BBS startup-script.

    assign altscr: doors:altscr


-Copy the contents of the archive to the altscr directory. 
 (executable, config and doc file)
 and edit the config file.
 If you want you can place screens in the altscr directory.

    copy ram:#?  altscr:
   
-Place the folowing in your logout or maintenance script.

    altscr:altscr >nil: altscr:cfg1

 If searching for errors you could use the folowing.

    altscr:altscr -d altscr:cfg1
 or
    altscr:altscr >>xlog:altscr.log -d altscr:cfg1

